# ===================================================================
# realmview fork additions
# ===================================================================
#
# Native plugin build artifacts produced by BuildScripts~/build_plugin_android.{sh,ps1}
# (and the other build_plugin_*.sh scripts under BuildScripts~/). All paths are
# anchored to the repo root with a leading slash so we don't accidentally ignore
# similarly-named files deeper in the tree.
#
# webrtc.zip is the prebuilt libwebrtc archive the build scripts download from
# the official Unity CDN (~7 MB compressed, ~700 MB extracted). It's a build
# cache and must never be committed -- the URL in the build scripts is the
# source of truth. Each build script reuses the cached zip if present; first
# run after `git clean -fdx` downloads it again.

/webrtc.zip
/webrtc.zip.meta

# build_log.txt is the per-build transcript captured by the PowerShell wrapper
# (build_plugin_android.ps1) and any other tee'd stdout/stderr from the bash
# build scripts. Useful for diagnosing build failures but never useful in git
# history -- the same information is on disk on whichever machine ran the
# build, and the next build overwrites it anyway.
/build_log.txt
/build_log.txt.meta

# OS-level clutter that is not covered by the Visual Studio template above.
# macOS Finder metadata and Windows folder-thumbnail cache should never be
# committed regardless of who is contributing to the fork.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unity auto-generated .meta files that upstream does NOT track
# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream tracks the *source* file but not the corresponding `.meta` that
# Unity creates the first time it scans this package. Until upstream commits
# those .meta files (which they may never -- these paths are not under
# Assets/ and don't strictly need them), every fork checkout regenerates
# them and they show up as untracked.
#
# We intentionally do NOT use a blanket `*.meta` rule because Unity-aware
# package paths (`Editor/`, `Runtime/`, `Tests/`, `Samples~/`,
# `Documentation~/`) DO require their .meta files to be checked in -- those
# are how Unity establishes asset GUIDs and import settings. Ignore only
# the specific paths where we know upstream doesn't track them:

# Root-level config files (legit Unity package files, but upstream skipped
# the .meta -- probably because they live outside Assets/ in the package).
/TestRunnerOptions.json.meta
/xray-exemptions.json.meta

# Tools/ contains the Wrench .NET tooling project. It is NOT a Unity Assets
# directory -- it's a standalone C# solution that Unity should not be
# scanning for assets. Ignore every .meta file under it so the local Unity
# scanner doesn't pollute the working tree.
/Tools.meta
/Tools/**/*.meta
